dent Oracle.\\ntools/rust-partition-poc/src/main.rs:32:    validate(&baseline, 20).expect(\\\"baseline oracle\\\");\\ntools/rust-partition-poc/src/main.rs:33:    println!(\\\"PASS partition invariant oracle: {:?}\\\", baseline);\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:4:row is covered only when its command, fixture, oracle and result log are linked.\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:6:| contract_id | scenario | execution entry | oracle | status |\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:8:| API-REST-001 | vertex CRUD and validation | `hugegraph-api` integration profile (to be pinned) | schema/error oracle | planned |\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:9:| API-GREMLIN-001 | traversal result and ordering | `hugegraph-test` core profile | public result oracle | planned |\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:10:| SCHEMA-001 | property/index uniqueness | core test profile | invariant oracle | planned |\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:11:| TXN-001 | commit/rollback visibility | core test profile | state-transition oracle | planned |\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:12:| RAFT-001 | replicated write under restart | `tools/raft-linearizability` harness | independent linearizability oracle | partial |\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:13:| SNAP-001 | snapshot export/import and corruption rejection | `tools/rust-rewrite-cluster/verify-snapshot-corruption.py` (negative component) | checksum/state oracle | partial |\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:17:independent single-register oracle exists but real three-node history capture is\\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/e2e-contract-matrix-20260913.md:21:stdout/stderr log, normalized result, oracle report, and (for mutation rows) a\\ntools/rust-partition-poc/README.md:3:This standalone model is an independent invariant oracle, deliberately separate from Java and any future Rust production implementation. `cargo test --manifest-path tools/rust-partition-poc/Cargo.toml` runs six deterministic checks: baseline validity, dropped range, overlap, version regression, stale heartbeat, and idempotent heartbeat.\\ntools/rust-partition-poc/README.md:5:The negative tests mutate the model input and must fail validation; they are evidence that the oracle detects the first three required defect classes. Cache loss, crash replay, and restart recovery remain integration tests against PD and are still NO-GO until executed with logs and fixed seeds.\\ntools/raft-linearizability/README.md:7:semantics. It is intentionally small and suitable as a test oracle.\\ntools/raft-linearizability/README.md:32:`compare_traces.py` is a dependency-free differential oracle. Give it Java and Rust replay traces (arrays or `{ \\\"operations\\\": [...] }`). It compares only `op`, `key`, `value`, and `result`, ignoring timestamps and implementation metadata.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/evidence/rust-rewrite/codex-loop.log.session-10:17:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"cat > docs/evidence/rust-rewrite/api-gremlin-001-independent-oracle-20260913.md <<'EOF'\\n# API-GREMLIN-001 independent oracle\\n\\nOracle source: \\\"'`TaskCoreTest` assertions in `hugegraph-server/hugegraph-test/src/main/java/org/apache/hugegraph/core/TaskCoreTest.java`.\\n\\nThe Java 11 execution evidence records both contract assertions passing: `testGremlinJob` requires task status `SUCCESS`, type `gremlin`, and result `8`; `testGremlinJobWithSerializedResults` requires the deterministic serialized traversal result string asserted by the test. The independent check is the test'\\\"'s persisted task reload assertion for \\\"'`testGremlinJob`, which verifies the same status/type/result after scheduler re-read.\\n\\nEvidence: `api-gremlin-